You can exercise an attribute or abuse an attribute (except for intelligence
or charisma).  Every so often, nethack checks which ones you've been 
exercising/abusing, and increases/decreases that stat by one.  This
check is made every rn1(200,800) moves.  Several laws of diminishing returns
apply, making it tough for your attributes to go up indefinitely.














<More Spoilers>














Many, many things are counted as exercise or abuse.  Here are a few examples:

Any good kick exercises dexterity.
Kicking at empty space abuses dexterity.
  if you strain a muscle, you abuse strength.
Kicking a wall abuses dexterity and strength.
Kicking a door open exercises strength.
  if the door explodes, you abuse strength.
Finding something exercises wisdom.
Learning a spell or casting it (successfully) exercises wisdom.
Forgeting spells (amnesia?) abuses wisdom.
Special monster attacks may abuse various things.
Successful encounters with succubus exercise various things
   (insert witty comment here)
Nurses exercise strength and constitution.
Attacking monsters bare handed exercises strength
Killing any monster exercises dexterity.
Successful sacrifices exercises wisdom.
Getting stuck in a trap abuses various attributes.
Pushing a boulder exercises strength.
...and many, many more.

The only thing that surprised me is that eating various things don't
seem to exercise anything.
